# Build a Master Archer and shoot the same target twice, once with a sling
# and once with a long bow. That is bd inc-tek.8.3 finding PA-03-F20: the
# class's Ranged Sneak Attack fired with every launcher in the game, not
# only with the bows its own description names.
#
# THE BUILD. The gate (lib/prestige.irh:2195-2232) wants an archery BAB of
# +5, Weapon Focus in a long bow or short bow, the Point Blank Shot, Rapid
# Shot and Zen Archery feats, Concentration 7, and either elven blood or
# Wisdom 17.
#   * A ranger attacks at 100% in archery, so five ranger levels are the
#     cheapest +5 (lib/classes.irh:2119).
#   * The archery combat style hands over Rapid Shot at 1st and Point Blank
#     Shot at 3rd for free (lib/classes.irh:2025-2027).
#   * Zen Archery needs Far Shot and Blind Fight first (src/FeatTab.cpp:1426),
#     and Blind Fight needs Wisdom 13 (:1392). Both are taken at creation.
#   * The ranger does NOT carry Concentration (lib/classes.irh:2120-2123), and
#     Character::MaxRanks caps a skill no class of yours carries at zero
#     ranks. The bard does carry it (lib/classes.irh:440), so three bard
#     levels open the skill.
#   * An elf needs no Wisdom score for the gate.
# Ranger 5 / Bard 3 / Master Archer 1 is nine levels, inside MAX_CHAR_LEVEL.
#
# Feats arrive at total level 1, 3, 6 and 9 (src/Create.cpp:2370), so the
# order is forced: Far Shot and Blind Fight at creation, Weapon Focus (long
# bow) at 3rd, Zen Archery at 6th.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Ranger"

# Point buy, 75 points, spent to the last one.
p
RIGHT*5         # STR 13
DOWN
RIGHT*10        # DEX 18
DOWN
RIGHT*7         # CON 15
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # INT 16
DOWN
RIGHT*10        # WIS 18, which Blind Fight and the Zen Archery chain want
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # CHA 16
DOWN
RIGHT*8         # LUC 16
ENTER y         # "Are these your final stats?"

@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Goblinkin"     # favoured enemy; any will do
a                       # Combat style: [a] archery
@choose "Far Shot"      # Zen Archery needs this one
@choose "Blind Fight"   # and this one
@while "Choose a feat" a

@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
# The list is alphabetical and the cursor only ever moves one way per
# directive, so the skills are visited in alphabetical order.
@cursorto:mark "Animal Empathy" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Climb" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Listen" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Ride" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
RIGHT*2
ENTER y

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
DOWN*8
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES. A frozen monster never takes a turn, so
        #   its FFCount never resets and it stays off-guard, which is the
        #   condition a sneak attack needs. It also cannot kill the archer
        #   between the three shots.
DOWN
SPACE   # Show All Combat Rolls: NO -> YES. This is what makes the engine
        #   print the "Damage:" line (src/Fight.cpp:8038), which is where
        #   a sneak attack writes its own " +Nd6 SA" term.
ESC

d       # character sheet
G       # Ranger 2
@while "Choose a feat" a
G       # Ranger 3 -- total level 3, so a feat is offered
# Weapon Focus sits past the 52nd row of the feat list, where LMenu has run
# out of letters and draws "[ ] Weapon Focus". Only the cursor can reach it.
@cursorto "Weapon Focus" DOWN
ENTER
@choose "long bow"
@while "Choose a feat" a
G       # Ranger 4 -- total level 4, so the attribute bonus is offered
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" c
@while "You feel hardier" ESC   # the pop-up that announces it eats the next key
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "Class  Ranger 5" G
@expect "Ranger 5"

M       # [M]ulticlass
@choose "Bard"

# Bard 1 is total level 6, so this level offers the last feat the gate needs.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Bard"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" c
@while "You feel hardier" ESC   # the pop-up that announces it eats the next key
@cursorto "Zen Archery" DOWN
ENTER
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Bard"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" c
@while "You feel hardier" ESC   # the pop-up that announces it eats the next key
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Bard"
@while "Learn which spell" a
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" c
@while "You feel hardier" ESC   # the pop-up that announces it eats the next key
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@expect "Bard 3"

# Concentration lives in the bard's list, not the ranger's, so the Skill
# Manager has to be turned to the bard page with TAB before the ranks show a
# cap above zero.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
TAB                             # turn the page from the ranger to the bard
# Three bard levels bring 36 ranks and the screen will not close while any
# are unspent, so eight skills are listed: enough capacity to absorb them all
# whatever the exact pool turns out to be. Concentration is the one the gate
# reads; the rest are ballast. The list is alphabetical and the cursor moves
# one way per directive, so they are visited in that order.
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Concentration" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Decipher Script" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Diplomacy" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*6
@cursorto:mark "Escape Artist" DOWN
RIGHT*6
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Master Archer"
@expect "Archer 0"              # the gate let him in

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Master Archer"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" c
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "Skill Ratings" d
@expect "Archer 1"
@dump:archer
# THE MEASUREMENT. The archer shoots the same kind of target twice: once with
# the long bow the class description names, and once with a sling. A sneak
# attack writes its own term into the damage line, " +Nd6 SA"
# (src/Fight.cpp:5135), and the wizard switch above makes that line print.
#
# WHY THE TARGET IS A FRESHLY SUMMONED MONSTER. Sneak attack damage needs the
# victim off-guard, flanked or surprised, and the attacker within three
# squares (src/Fight.cpp:5113-5115). Monster::Initialize sets FFCount to 20
# on every new monster (src/Monster.cpp:1446) and isFlatFooted() is
# FFCount > 5, so a monster is off-guard on the turn it appears. Summoning
# one beside the archer makes the condition certain rather than lucky.
#
# EVERY ITEM IS MADE IN WIZARD MODE AND PLACED STRAIGHT FROM THE AIR. Nothing
# is fetched out of the pack: the pack list scrolls, and a cursor directive
# cannot reach a row that has scrolled off it.
@until "HP:" ESC

# The elven long bow +2 he was born with goes into the Weapon Hand. Its iID
# is still $"long bow", which is the name the corrected test looks for.
# A slot letter only moves the cursor; SPACE lifts an item into the
# In-the-Air slot and puts it down again, so each move is a pair.
i
e SPACE         # lift the long bow out of the L. Shoulder slot
b SPACE         # put it in the Weapon Hand; the long sword comes out
@until "Air':Empty" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

# Arrows in the pack are not "ready" -- the fire command says so in as many
# words -- so a fresh sheaf goes straight into the L. Shoulder slot the bow
# has just left. Sheaf arrows are the first entry under Missiles.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Missiles" RIGHT
ENTER
e SPACE
@until "Air':Empty" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

# THE CONTROL SHOT: a long bow, which is what the class description allows.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Giants"
@choose "ogre"
RIGHT ENTER
f
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Take opportunity" n
@while "Confirm bludgeon" n
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" d
@while "--More--" ENTER
v
@dump:bowlog
ESC

# TEST SHOT ONE: a sling. Each shot gets its own freshly summoned ogre,
# because a strike resets the victim's FFCount to zero (src/Fight.cpp:3040)
# and a monster that has been shot at once is no longer off-guard.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Missile Weapons" RIGHT
DOWN*6
ENTER
b SPACE         # the sling into the Weapon Hand; the bow comes out
d               # and the bow on the floor. It will neither stow nor go in
                #   the Ready Hand -- it is two-handed -- and the game
                #   refuses to leave inventory mode with anything in the air.
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Missiles" RIGHT
DOWN*5
ENTER
e SPACE         # stones into the L. Shoulder slot, where the arrows were
d               # and the arrows on the floor, beside the bow that fired them
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Giants"
@choose "ogre"
LEFT ENTER
f
LEFT ENTER
@while "Take opportunity" n
@while "Confirm bludgeon" n
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" d
@while "--More--" ENTER
v
@dump:slinglog
ESC

# TEST SHOT TWO: an arbalest. A crossbow is unambiguously the generic
# launcher attack type -- inc/Defines.h:1185 names the constant
# "Fire [Cross]bow". The arbalest rather than the hand crossbow, because the
# acquisition list offers no hand crossbow darts and that weapon will not
# shoot a bolt.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Missile Weapons" RIGHT
DOWN*2
ENTER
b SPACE         # the arbalest into the Weapon Hand; the sling comes out
d               # and the sling on the floor beside the bow
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Missiles" RIGHT
DOWN*2
ENTER
e SPACE
d
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

# A crossbow has to be cranked before it will shoot, and cranking costs one
# fire command, so it is spent before the third ogre exists.
f
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Take opportunity" n
@while "Confirm bludgeon" n
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" d
@while "--More--" ENTER

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Giants"
@choose "ogre"
DOWN ENTER
f
DOWN ENTER
@while "Take opportunity" n
@while "Confirm bludgeon" n
@while "Abort, Flee or Disengage" d
@while "--More--" ENTER
v
@dump:crossbowlog
ESC

@quit
